ation, treatment, and outcomes of Riedel's thyroiditis.", "EGSGAARD NIELSEN V:Egsgaard Nielsen V is an author of a case report on a rare case of orbital involvement in Riedel's thyroiditis.", "TSH-SECRETING PITUITARY ADENOMAS:TSH-secreting pituitary adenomas are tumors that produce excess thyroid-stimulating hormone, which can lead to hyperthyroidism.", "CLINICAL GUIDELINES:Clinical guidelines are systematically developed statements designed to assist both practitioners and patients in making informed decisions regarding appropriate healthcare for specific clinical circumstances. These guidelines encompass a wide range of medical conditions and provide evidence-based recommendations tailored for healthcare professionals. For instance, clinical guidelines for the management of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis offer targeted recommendations to improve patient care. Additionally, they include protocols for the diagnosis and treatment of conditions such as incidental pituitary adenomas, as well as management strategies for hyponatremia, addressing various severity levels. Overall, clinical guidelines serve as a crucial resource in ensuring effective and standardized healthcare practices.", "PITUITARY TUMOR:", "FALHAMMAR ET AL.:Falhammar et al. es un grupo de investigadores que realizaron una serie reciente sobre la tiroiditis de Riedel, presentando datos sobre la positividad de anticuerpos en pacientes.", "KAKUDO ET AL.:Kakudo et al. es un grupo de investigadores que estudiaron el diagnóstico de la tiroiditis de Hashimoto y la enfermedad esclerosante relacionada con IgG4.", "HENNESSEY JV.:Hennessey JV. es un autor que realizó una revisión clínica sobre la tiroiditis de Riedel, abordando su presentación y tratamiento.", "HARTEMANN ET AL.:Hartemann et al. es un grupo de investigadores que documentaron un caso de tiroiditis de Riedel regresiva.", "CIBAS ES:Cibas ES is an author who has significantly contributed to the development of the Bethesda system for the classification 